{"availability":"available","full":"meslater1030/web-audio-api-sample","name":"web-audio-api-sample","description":"Demo App for Web Audio API Functionality","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2018-02-20T01:32:43Z","updated":"2019-04-11T02:19:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["javascript","material-ui","react","webaudio-api"],"demo":"https://mdn.github.io/voice-change-o-matic/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:57.866Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:57.866Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:57.866Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:07:57.866Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["As browsers become more and more the de facto platform for software of all kinds an increasing number of technologies have become widespread across all browsers. Included in that is the native JavaScript Web Audio API. Everything you see here is possible using native JavaScript in modern web browsers. There is no audio library to import, there is no WebAssembly to use. This particular app is built using React just for the sake of having a nice display.","This app contains some samples of what is possible using a few basic Web Audio API functionalities. Every sample comes with some example code, just click on the button next to that sample.","Note: Before trying out any functionality using microphone input (voice) be sure that your microphone is not located near your speakers. This will cause feedback. An easy workaround on your own device is to use headphones."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/meslater1030/web-audio-api-sample/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"9b372a210544d53b12055c2792592fc16eee419b014cc6354fc497243f992622","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:57.975Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:57.975Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"As browsers become more and m